  "id": "COMPOUND:24335 - PROTEIN:5854",
  "verbalization": "Peperomin B is implicated in the biological activity of LNCaP cells through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Peperomin B acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, both of which are known to target Carboxylesterase 2 and subsequently LNCaP. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism by which Peperomin B influences LNCaP cell behavior, possibly through the modulation of enzyme activity or the activation of downstream signaling pathways. The shared target of Peperomin B and LNCaP suggests a possible dependency on these compounds, reinforcing the notion that Peperomin B may exert its effects via a common molecular mechanism involving Carboxylesterase 2. The integration of these pathways underscores the complexity of the interaction, with Peperomin B potentially acting as a bridge between the compound and the cellular response in LNCaP.",
